=== meta ===
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
title: a repository guard on the test job is a condition, not a disabled job
origin: issue #181 bound — `github.repository == ...` is unknown statically, and fork guards
origin2: are routine, so the job stays live and the edit stays the existing warn.
=== before: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: "3.12"
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest
=== after: .github/workflows/ci.yml ===
name: ci
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
jobs:
  test:
    if: github.repository == 'acme/billing'
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: "3.12"
      - run: pip install -e .
      - run: pytest
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "warn"}]
